<Placemark><name>Jerusalem</name><styleUrl>#city</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Identified with:</b> Jerusalem</p><p><b>Confidence:</b> Very likely (100% of current scholarship)</p><p><b>Mentioned</b> 955 times, first in Joshua 10:1.</p><p><b>Books:</b> Joshua (9), Judges (4), 1 Samuel (1), 2 Samuel (37), 1 Kings (30), 2 Kings (61), 1 Chronicles (28), 2 Chronicles (122), Ezra (51), Nehemiah (35), Esther (1), Psalms (38), Ecclesiastes (5), Song of Songs (8), Isaiah (73), Jeremiah (133), Lamentations (15), Ezekiel (44), Daniel (10), Joel (6), Amos (2), Obadiah (3), Micah (12), Zephaniah (7), Zechariah (42), Malachi (2), Matthew (15), Mark (14), Luke (38), John (18), Acts (70), Romans (5), 1 Corinthians (2), 2 Corinthians (4), Galatians (5), Hebrews (1), Revelation (4)</p><p><b>Also called:</b> Ariel, Jebus, Salem, The Lord Is There, Zion</p><p><b>Places within:</b> Angle, Baal-hamon, Beautiful Gate, Benjamin Gate, Corner Gate, Dung Gate, East Gate, East Square, Ephraim Gate, Fish Gate, Fountain Gate, Gareb, Gate of Yeshanah, Gate of the Foundation, Gate of the Guard, Horse Gate, House of the Forest of Lebanon, Lower Pool, Middle Gate, Millo, Mortar, Muster Gate, New Gate, North Gate, Old Pool, Parbar, People’s Gate, Potsherd Gate, Second Quarter, Shallecheth, Sheep Gate, Solomon’s Portico, South Gate, Tower of the Ovens, Upper Pool, Uzza, Valley Gate, Water Gate</p><p><b>Other translations:</b> daughter of Judah, City of the Lord, Daughter Judah, Zion, Judah, daughter Judah</p><p><a href="https://hj367.github.io/bible-places/#jerusalem">Open Jerusalem in the All Bible Places atlas</a></p><p><a href="https://www.openbible.info/geo/ancient/a15257a/jerusalem">Sources on OpenBible.info</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>35.23417,31.77667,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Babylon</name><styleUrl>#city</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Identified with:</b> Babylon</p><p><b>Confidence:</b> Very likely (100% of current scholarship)</p><p><b>Mentioned</b> 296 times, first in 2 Kings 17:24.</p><p><b>Books:</b> 2 Kings (29), 1 Chronicles (1), 2 Chronicles (8), Ezra (9), Nehemiah (2), Esther (1), Psalms (4), Isaiah (24), Jeremiah (171), Ezekiel (22), Daniel (17), Micah (1), Zechariah (3), Matthew (3), Acts (1)</p><p><b>Also called:</b> Babel, Merathaim, Sheshach</p><p><b>Other translations:</b> Babylonia, Babylonians, Babylonian, Desert by the Sea, Tyre, Wilderness of the Sea</p><p><a href="https://hj367.github.io/bible-places/#babylon-1">Open Babylon in the All Bible Places atlas</a></p><p><a href="https://www.openbible.info/geo/ancient/a217d18/babylon-1">Sources on OpenBible.info</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>44.42222,32.54333,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Samaria</name><styleUrl>#city</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Identified with:</b> Samaria</p><p><b>Confidence:</b> Very likely (100% of current scholarship)</p><p><b>Mentioned</b> 113 times, first in 1 Kings 13:32.</p><p><b>Books:</b> 1 Kings (17), 2 Kings (49), 2 Chronicles (8), Ezra (2), Nehemiah (1), Isaiah (9), Jeremiah (3), Ezekiel (7), Hosea (6), Amos (6), Obadiah (1), Micah (4)</p><p><b>Also called:</b> Shamir</p><p><b>Other translations:</b> Mount Samaria, Samaritans, Samarian</p><p><a href="https://hj367.github.io/bible-places/#samaria-1">Open Samaria in the All Bible Places atlas</a></p><p><a href="https://www.openbible.info/geo/ancient/a041bb3/samaria-1">Sources on OpenBible.info</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>35.195,32.27611,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Bethel</name><styleUrl>#city</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Identified with:</b> Beitin</p><p><b>Confidence:</b> Likely (72% of current scholarship)</p><p><b>Other proposed sites:</b> Al Bira (10%); Burj Beitin (0%)</p><p><b>Mentioned</b> 69 times, first in Genesis 12:8.</p><p><b>Books:</b> Genesis (12), Joshua (10), Judges (10), 1 Samuel (3), 1 Kings (11), 2 Kings (10), 1 Chronicles (1), 2 Chronicles (1), Ezra (1), Nehemiah (2), Hosea (2), Amos (6)</p><p><b>Also called:</b> Beth-aven, Bochim, Luz</p><p><b>Places within:</b> El-bethel</p><p><b>Other translations:</b> Beth-el, Bethelite, Beth-elite</p><p><a href="https://hj367.github.io/bible-places/#bethel-1">Open Bethel in the All Bible Places atlas</a></p><p><a href="https://www.openbible.info/geo/ancient/a64f355/bethel-1">Sources on OpenBible.info</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>35.24139,31.92278,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Tyre</name><styleUrl>#city</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Identified with:</b> Tyre</p><p><b>Confidence:</b> Very likely (100% of current scholarship)</p><p><b>Mentioned</b> 64 times, first in Joshua 19:29.</p><p><b>Books:</b> Joshua (1), 2 Samuel (2), 1 Kings (5), 1 Chronicles (2), 2 Chronicles (3), Ezra (1), Nehemiah (1), Psalms (3), Isaiah (8), Jeremiah (3), Ezekiel (15), Hosea (1), Joel (1), Amos (2), Zechariah (4), Matthew (3), Mark (3), Luke (3), Acts (3)</p><p><b>Other translations:</b> Tyrus, Tyrians, Tyrian, Zemer</p><p><a href="https://hj367.github.io/bible-places/#tyre">Open Tyre in the All Bible Places atlas</a></p><p><a href="https://www.openbible.info/geo/ancient/a160272/tyre">Sources on OpenBible.info</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>35.19611,33.27083,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Jericho</name><styleUrl>#city</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Identified with:</b> Tell es Sultan</p><p><b>Confidence:</b> Very likely (100% of current scholarship)</p><p><b>Mentioned</b> 63 times, first in Numbers 22:1.</p><p><b>Books:</b> Numbers (9), Deuteronomy (3), Joshua (31), Judges (2), 2 Samuel (1), 1 Kings (1), 2 Kings (7), 1 Chronicles (2), 2 Chronicles (1), Ezra (1), Nehemiah (2), Jeremiah (2), Hebrews (1)</p><p><b>Also called:</b> City of Palms</p><p><a href="https://hj367.github.io/bible-places/#jericho-1">Open Jericho in the All Bible Places atlas</a></p><p><a href="https://www.openbible.info/geo/ancient/a231f80/jericho-1">Sources on OpenBible.info</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>35.44456,31.87172,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Hebron</name><styleUrl>#city</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Identified with:</b> Tel Rumeida</p><p><b>Confidence:</b> Very likely (100% of current scholarship)</p><p><b>Mentioned</b> 62 times, first in Genesis 13:18.</p><p><b>Books:</b> Genesis (4), Numbers (1), Joshua (17), Judges (3), 1 Samuel (1), 2 Samuel (24), 1 Kings (1), 1 Chronicles (9), 2 Chronicles (1), Nehemiah (1)</p><p><b>Other translations:</b> Kiriath-arba, Kiriath Arba, Kirjath Arba, Kirjath-arba, Arba, Kiriath-Arba</p><p><a href="https://hj367.github.io/bible-places/#hebron">Open Hebron in the All Bible Places atlas</a></p><p><a href="https://www.openbible.info/geo/ancient/a85151a/hebron">Sources on OpenBible.info</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>35.10222,31.52509,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Damascus</name><styleUrl>#city</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Identified with:</b> Damascus</p><p><b>Confidence:</b> Very likely (100% of current scholarship)</p><p><b>Mentioned</b> 58 times, first in Genesis 14:15.</p><p><b>Books:</b> Genesis (2), 2 Samuel (2), 1 Kings (4), 2 Kings (8), 1 Chronicles (2), 2 Chronicles (4), Song of Songs (1), Isaiah (5), Jeremiah (3), Ezekiel (5), Amos (4), Zechariah (2), Acts (14), 2 Corinthians (1), Galatians (1)</p><p><b>Other translations:</b> Wilderness of Damascus, Desert of Damascus, Syria-damascus</p><p><a href="https://hj367.github.io/bible-places/#damascus">Open Damascus in the All Bible Places atlas</a></p><p><a href="https://www.openbible.info/geo/ancient/a69c1d4/damascus">Sources on OpenBible.info</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>36.30639,33.51111,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Bethlehem</name><styleUrl>#city</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Identified with:</b> Bethlehem</p><p><b>Confidence:</b> Very likely (100% of current scholarship)</p><p><b>Mentioned</b> 52 times, first in Genesis 35:19.</p><p><b>Books:</b> Genesis (2), Judges (7), Ruth (7), 1 Samuel (8), 2 Samuel (6), 1 Chronicles (7), 2 Chronicles (1), Ezra (1), Nehemiah (1), Jeremiah (1), Micah (1), Matthew (6), Luke (3), John (1)</p><p><b>Also called:</b> Ephrath, Ephrathah</p><p><b>Other translations:</b> Beth-lehem, Bethlehemite, Beth-lehem-judah, Bethlehem Ephrathah, Beth-lehemite, Beth-lehem Ephratah</p><p><a href="https://hj367.github.io/bible-places/#bethlehem-1">Open Bethlehem in the All Bible Places atlas</a></p><p><a href="https://www.openbible.info/geo/ancient/a112427/bethlehem-1">Sources on OpenBible.info</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>35.20764,31.70431,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Sodom</name><styleUrl>#city-u</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Identified with:</b> In the Valley of Siddim</p><p><b>Confidence:</b> Possible (39% of current scholarship)</p><p><b>Other proposed sites:</b> Bab edh Dhra (14%); in the region north of the Dead Sea (12%); Tall el Hammam (3%); Numeira (-2%)</p><p><b>Mentioned</b> 50 times, first in Genesis 10:19.</p><p><b>Books:</b> Genesis (20), Deuteronomy (2), Isaiah (4), Jeremiah (3), Lamentations (1), Ezekiel (7), Amos (1), Zephaniah (1), Matthew (3), Mark (1), Luke (2), Romans (1), 2 Peter (2), Jude (1), Revelation (1)</p><p><b>Other translations:</b> Sodoma</p><p><a href="https://hj367.github.io/bible-places/#sodom">Open Sodom in the All Bible Places atlas</a></p><p><a href="https://www.openbible.info/geo/ancient/a0aa664/sodom">Sources on OpenBible.info</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>35.44922,31.20849,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>City of David</name><styleUrl>#city</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Identified with:</b> City of David</p><p><b>Confidence:</b> Very likely (100% of current scholarship)</p><p><b>Mentioned</b> 46 times, first in 2 Samuel 5:7.</p><p><b>Books:</b> 2 Samuel (5), 1 Kings (10), 2 Kings (7), 1 Chronicles (5), 2 Chronicles (15), Nehemiah (2), Isaiah (2)</p><p><b>Other translations:</b> city of David, city of his father David, city of his ancestor David, city of Judah, city where David encamped, City of Judah</p><p><a href="https://hj367.github.io/bible-places/#city-of-david">Open City of David in the All Bible Places atlas</a></p><p><a href="https://www.openbible.info/geo/ancient/a84f426/city-of-david">Sources on OpenBible.info</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>35.23556,31.77361,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Gibeah</name><styleUrl>#city</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Identified with:</b> Tel el Ful</p><p><b>Confidence:</b> Likely (67% of current scholarship)</p><p><b>Other proposed sites:</b> another name for Geba 1 (9%); Jaba (3%)</p><p><b>Mentioned</b> 45 times, first in Judges 19:12.</p><p><b>Books:</b> Judges (23), 1 Samuel (12), 2 Samuel (4), 1 Chronicles (2), Isaiah (1), Hosea (3)</p><p><b>Also called:</b> Gibeath-elohim</p><p><b>Other translations:</b> Gibeathite, Gibeon, Geba, Gibeonite</p><p><a href="https://hj367.github.io/bible-places/#gibeah-1">Open Gibeah in the All Bible Places atlas</a></p><p><a href="https://www.openbible.info/geo/ancient/ac24f5f/gibeah-1">Sources on OpenBible.info</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>35.23072,31.82311,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Shechem</name><styleUrl>#city</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Identified with:</b> Tell Balatah</p><p><b>Confidence:</b> Very likely (100% of current scholarship)</p><p><b>Mentioned</b> 45 times, first in Genesis 12:6.</p><p><b>Books:</b> Genesis (6), Joshua (6), Judges (23), 1 Kings (2), 1 Chronicles (2), 2 Chronicles (1), Psalms (2), Jeremiah (1), Hosea (1), Acts (1)</p><p><b>Places within:</b> Beth-millo, Tower of Shechem</p><p><b>Other translations:</b> Shechemites, Sichem, Sychem</p><p><a href="https://hj367.github.io/bible-places/#shechem">Open Shechem in the All Bible Places atlas</a></p><p><a href="https://www.openbible.info/geo/ancient/adf74d4/shechem">Sources on OpenBible.info</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>35.28194,32.21361,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Gibeon</name><styleUrl>#city</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Identified with:</b> El Jib</p><p><b>Confidence:</b> Very likely (91% of current scholarship)</p><p><b>Mentioned</b> 39 times, first in Joshua 9:3.</p><p><b>Books:</b> Joshua (14), 2 Samuel (7), 1 Kings (3), 1 Chronicles (7), 2 Chronicles (3), Nehemiah (2), Jeremiah (3)</p><p><b>Also called:</b> Geba</p><p><b>Other translations:</b> Gibeonites, Gibeonite, Gibbar, Wilderness of Gibeon</p><p><a href="https://hj367.github.io/bible-places/#gibeon">Open Gibeon in the All Bible Places atlas</a></p><p><a href="https://www.openbible.info/geo/ancient/aede336/gibeon">Sources on OpenBible.info</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>35.18335,31.84745,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Gath</name><styleUrl>#city</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Identified with:</b> Tell es Safi</p><p><b>Confidence:</b> Very likely (85% of current scholarship)</p><p><b>Other proposed sites:</b> Tel Nagila (4%); Tell esh Sharia (4%); Ras Abu Hamid (1%); Tel Haror (-2%)</p><p><b>Mentioned</b> 38 times, first in Joshua 11:22.</p><p><b>Books:</b> Joshua (2), 1 Samuel (15), 2 Samuel (8), 1 Kings (3), 2 Kings (1), 1 Chronicles (4), 2 Chronicles (2), Psalms (1), Amos (1), Micah (1)</p><p><b>Also called:</b> Metheg-ammah</p><p><b>Other translations:</b> Gittite, Gittites</p><p><a href="https://hj367.github.io/bible-places/#gath-1">Open Gath in the All Bible Places atlas</a></p><p><a href="https://www.openbible.info/geo/ancient/a18873f/gath-1">Sources on OpenBible.info</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>34.84694,31.69972,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
