<Placemark><name>Mount Seir</name><styleUrl>#mountain</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Identified with:</b> Region around Jebel esh Shera</p><p><b>Confidence:</b> Likely (78% of current scholarship)</p><p><b>Other proposed sites:</b> mountains southwest of the Dead Sea (7%)</p><p><b>Mentioned</b> 34 times, first in Genesis 14:6.</p><p><b>Books:</b> Genesis (7), Numbers (1), Deuteronomy (10), Joshua (3), Judges (1), 1 Chronicles (1), 2 Chronicles (5), Isaiah (1), Ezekiel (5)</p><p><b>Also called:</b> Mount Esau</p><p><b>Other translations:</b> Seir, hill country of Seir, mountain of Seir, Seirites, Edom, Edomites</p><p><a href="https://hj367.github.io/bible-places/#mount-seir-1">Open Mount Seir in the All Bible Places atlas</a></p><p><a href="https://www.openbible.info/geo/ancient/ae981db/mount-seir-1">Sources on OpenBible.info</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>35.3166,30.1843,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
