<Placemark><name>Valley of Eshcol</name><styleUrl>#mountain-n</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Identified with:</b> Within 5 km of Hebron</p><p><b>Confidence:</b> Likely (59% of current scholarship)</p><p><b>Other proposed sites:</b> region around Burj el Haska (10%); region around Ain Eshkali (8%); within 2 km of Mamre (0%)</p><p><b>Mentioned</b> 4 times, first in Numbers 13:23.</p><p><b>Books:</b> Numbers (3), Deuteronomy (1)</p><p><b>Other translations:</b> valley of Eshcol, Eshcol Valley, Valley of Eshkol, Wadi Eshcol, Eshcol, wadi of Eschol</p><p><a href="https://hj367.github.io/bible-places/#valley-of-eshcol">Open Valley of Eshcol in the All Bible Places atlas</a></p><p><a href="https://www.openbible.info/geo/ancient/a38ecff/valley-of-eshcol">Sources on OpenBible.info</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>35.10222,31.52509,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Akrabbim</name><styleUrl>#mountain-n</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<p><b>Identified with:</b> Ma’ale Akrabbim</p><p><b>Confidence:</b> Likely (73% of current scholarship)</p><p><b>Other proposed sites:</b> Jebel Umm al Aqarib (4%)</p><p><b>Mentioned</b> 3 times, first in Numbers 34:4.</p><p><b>Books:</b> Numbers (1), Joshua (1), Judges (1)</p><p><b>Other translations:</b> Scorpion Pass, Ascent of Akrabbim, Scorpion Ascent, Scorpions’ Ascent, Maaleh-acrabbim</p><p><a href="https://hj367.github.io/bible-places/#akrabbim">Open Akrabbim in the All Bible Places atlas</a></p><p><a href="https://www.openbible.info/geo/ancient/a39267b/akrabbim">Sources on OpenBible.info</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>35.13126,30.9066,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
